@@section 1
@@title CQ-SINK Visual sinking: no bump between sunken blocks, even depth, items on top, 2026-11-10 ([blockrunner.md](../blockrunner.md) 3.4, TODO `gameplay/blockrunner #7`)
@@date 2026-11-10
@@jars creativecompat creativedevtools
@@sources feature_writeup/blockrunner.md
@@text
@@text Needs the 2026-11-10 Creative Compat jar in `mods/`. Client only (rendering); default `[surface.sinking] depthPixels = 2`, raise to 8 to see it easily.
@@text
@@table
## CQ-SINK-01
@group client
@commands BR-53 and BR-55: first person, walk slowly slime -> honey -> slime, wool -> mud -> wool, wool -> dirt path; walk to a wool edge over a 1-block drop
@pass LOOK: no upward pop at any seam; at the edge the view stays sunk until you fall
@fails `SinkingRender.depthAt` corner fallback; `support` top check
@owner true
@draft walking feel across seams and a ledge (BR-53, BR-55): a person judges the view in motion; a `walk` step plus shots could stage it, but the pass is a feel
## CQ-SINK-02
@group client
@commands BR-54: F5, a pig on wool beside a pig on a honey block
@pass LOOK: equal depth
@fails `support` own-sink branch
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# side by side in front of the player (yaw 0 faces +z; at yaw 90 both pigs were out of view, one behind the other)
> fill ~-3 ~-1 ~4 ~-1 ~-1 ~4 minecraft:white_wool
> fill ~1 ~-1 ~4 ~3 ~-1 ~4 minecraft:honey_block
> summon minecraft:pig ~-2 ~ ~4 {NoAI:1b}
> summon minecraft:pig ~2 ~ ~4 {NoAI:1b}
do {"look": {"yaw": 0, "pitch": 10}}
do {"wait": 20}
shot pigs_side
look the two pigs sink to equal depth (the F5 third-person view of the row is the same judgement on any pig)
## CQ-SINK-03
@group client
@commands BR-56: drop items on wool, sand, slime; then add sand to `creativecompat:sinking_hides_items` in `blocktags.js`, `/reload`
@pass LOOK: items lie on the texture; after the edit the sand item sinks in, wool unchanged; revert the edit
@fails `HIDES_ITEMS` check in `support`; ItemPhysic renders through `EntityRenderDispatcher#render`
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> setblock ~ ~-1 ~3 minecraft:white_wool
> setblock ~2 ~-1 ~3 minecraft:sand
> setblock ~-2 ~-1 ~3 minecraft:slime_block
> summon minecraft:item ~ ~1 ~3 {Item:{id:"minecraft:apple",Count:1b}}
> summon minecraft:item ~2 ~1 ~3 {Item:{id:"minecraft:apple",Count:1b}}
> summon minecraft:item ~-2 ~1 ~3 {Item:{id:"minecraft:apple",Count:1b}}
do {"look": {"yaw": 0, "pitch": 35}}
do {"wait": 40}
shot items_on_blocks
look items lie on the texture of wool, sand and slime. The tag-edit half (add sand to `creativecompat:sinking_hides_items` in blocktags.js, /reload, the sand item sinks in, revert) edits a pack script: do it by hand in the same session
